      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a draft of the \"Getting Started\" guide for NexusCore:\n\n**Getting Started with NexusCore**\n=====================================\n\nThis guide will help you get started with using the NexusCore API to interact with our application. If you have any questions or need further assistance, please don't hesitate to reach out to our support team.\n\n### Authentication\n\nTo access the NexusCore API, you will need to authenticate with a valid API key. You can obtain a key by creating an account on our website or by contacting our support team. Once you have your key, you can use it in the `Authorization` header of your requests. For example:\n```http\nAuthorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY\n```\n### Making Your First Request\n\nTo retrieve data from the NexusCore API, you can start with a simple GET request to `https://api.nexuscore.com/resources`. Here is an example using [cURL](https://curl.se/):\n```bash\ncurl -X GET \\\n  https://api.nexuscore.com/resources \\\n  -H 'Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY' \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json'\n```\nThis will return a JSON response containing a list of available resources. You can then",
